{"@timestamp":"2026-10-09T00:39:17.539893Z","actor":"agent:transluce-ingest","body":{"basis":"UPSTREAM","cites":["observation_ce719f832a434e4f8f46e29a4d3c5057","observation_3ca0a26863d340f4b44be2278d89c772","observation_bbac2fdee2a848bc877a4419d986956c","observation_8d110ba70b9e4d3090360edd38dac145","observation_8f68f5ee625b4bc3a8d36cdbc4e18de0","observation_f0a6b39e3e8c4764ad287acad88048e7","observation_5fbbbd862b8d4f16a2f68556d0a16824"],"note":"Transluce findings tracker. Builds on #81 (Laura, Sep 28), which inventories ntfy.sh agent activity from a local evidence set: the 40-topic Tomas Kopecky search burst (matching BrowseComp 339; dated July 6 by this census) and all 37 July 8 input/output pairs, with go/START/OK markers labelled low-confidence. Also references #62 (early ntfy usage), #131 (a fleet using paste.rs plus one ntfy tally) and #116 (archival-site workflows). This finding is a methods extension, not a new activity claim: the runs belong to #81. Data ","property":"reported","subject":"observable_4178ea63abe4482f9f2178490754ce10","value":"Methods extension of #81: 90 ntfy.sh topics from its July runs were archived within 1 second of posting, so Wayback replays preserve exact message times and recover expired content. Also documents the go-signal ladder preceding the July 6 START wave."},"fingerprint":"60fc26fe66cc8a35689a5f605a2faffd5564fd1730fd135ecc9e5781f99cebc6","id":"claim_d2200df5182049b68147064980a74a74","record_kind":"claim","schema":"urn:factum:core:claim:1","tags":{"ai_company":"Unknown","novelty-check":true,"submitter":"Omer Zamir"}}
